---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import TalkBanner from '../components/TalkBanner.astro';
import LegalDoc from '../components/LegalDoc.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';
import { withBase } from '../config/paths';

// Draft. "If you become a client" was added 2026-11-17 for the solicitor's review. The retention
// periods (12 months after launch, 12 months for enquiries) are defaults to confirm with Gurman;
// HMRC's record-keeping rule for sole traders sets the invoice one. The storage it describes
// (private GitHub repositories, encrypted computers) must be true before the first client.
---

<BaseLayout page="privacy">
  <SiteHeader slot="header" />

  <LegalDoc
    title="Privacy notice"
    updated="23 November 2026"
    note="Draft: this notice has not been reviewed by a solicitor yet. It describes the site as it works today. The section on clients was added on 17 November 2026."
  >
    <h2>Who this covers</h2>
    <p>
      This notice covers this website and the information we handle for clients, run by{' '}
      {site.founder} trading as {site.name} (a working name — see the footer for current contact
      details). Gurman has not yet registered as a sole trader; that is planned before any paid work
      begins.
    </p>

    <h2>This site itself</h2>
    <p>
      The public pages set no cookies and run no analytics, advertising or tracking scripts of any
      kind. Visiting them does not create an account, a session or a tracking profile. Clients we
      work with can log in to a private client area, described below. If analytics are added later,
      this notice will be updated first and a cookie or consent notice will be added if required.
    </p>

    <h2>Hosting</h2>
    <p>
      This site is hosted by Cloudflare, which briefly processes standard request details (your IP
      address, browser type and the page asked for) to deliver the page and protect the site from
      abuse. We don't use those logs to track or profile anyone.
    </p>

    <h2>If you use a form</h2>
    <p>
      The contact form and the free AI check form ask for your name, an email to reply to, and
      optionally your website, phone number and a message. When you press send, those details are
      passed through Cloudflare and emailed straight to our inbox (Gmail, run by Google). A copy is
      also kept in our private enquiries list (a Cloudflare D1 database), which only the Hu/man team
      can see, so no enquiry gets lost. We use them only to answer you. We delete enquiries after 12
      months, unless you become a client, when they become part of the project record. Our lawful
      basis is our legitimate interest in replying to an enquiry you started.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you give a website address, we load that site's public home page, robots.txt and llms.txt
      once, automatically, and add a short summary to the email (its title, how quickly it answered
      and whether it lets AI crawlers in). That is information about the website, not about you.
    </p>
    <p>The forms include a hidden field that catches spam bots; it collects nothing about you.</p>

    <h2>If you call, email or message us directly</h2>
    <p>
      The email address and phone number open your own email app or dialler. That message goes
      directly from your device to us, the same as if you'd looked up the details yourself, and is
      handled like any other enquiry.
    </p>

    <h2>If you become a client</h2>
    <p>
      To build your site we use what you send us. For a CV or portfolio site that is usually your
      work history, qualifications, a photo and contact details, and sometimes the names or words of
      people you quote. We use it only to build, launch and look after your site, and our lawful
      basis is that we need it to carry out our contract with you. Anything you choose to show on
      your finished site is public once it goes live.
    </p>
    <p>
      Project files and messages are kept in our email (Gmail, run by Google), in private code
      repositories on GitHub and on our own encrypted computers, and your live site is hosted by
      Cloudflare. If a project needs any other service, we tell you which one first. Some of these
      companies may process data outside the UK; where they do, they use the safeguards UK law
      requires. We never put your photos or details into AI tools without asking you first.
    </p>
    <p>
      We keep your project files for 12 months after your site goes live, so we can fix anything
      that comes up, and then delete them. If we host or look after your site, we keep what we need
      for as long as we do. Invoices and payment records are kept for as long as HMRC requires.
      Enquiries that don't become projects are deleted within 12 months.
    </p>
    <p>
      Any project involving an AI assistant, booking system or similar tool will have its own,
      specific explanation of what data is collected, which providers process it, and how long it is
      kept, agreed with you before launch. Health-related businesses (for example dental or
      physiotherapy clients) get extra care here, in line with the rules for special-category data.
    </p>

    <h2>If you have an account</h2>
    <p>
      Anyone can create an account to ask for a portfolio, and we also make accounts for clients
      we're working with. An account holds your name, your email address and your password (stored
      only in a scrambled form we can't read back). If you sign in with Google or Microsoft instead,
      they tell us only your name, your email address, whether they've confirmed that email, and an
      account number that's yours with them; your Google or Microsoft password never reaches us.
      When you send a portfolio request it also holds what you put in the form (your name, contact
      details, job history, education, skills and any links), your CV if you upload one, and any
      portfolio we build for you. We never ask for your street address. We use all of this to make,
      deliver and look after your portfolio; the lawful basis is that we need it to do what you've
      asked us to, under our contract with you.
    </p>
    <p>
      It is stored with Cloudflare, in their database and file storage, in Europe. Emails to you
      (the code that confirms your email, password resets and "we've got your request") are sent by
      Resend, which handles your email address and the message only to deliver it. When you send a
      request, a summary is emailed to our inbox (Gmail). If you pay by card, the payment is handled
      by Stripe, which processes your card details as its own controller under its own privacy
      policy; we only see the amount, the date and whether it went through. Logging in sets one
      cookie that keeps you logged in: see the <a href={withBase('/cookies/')}>cookie policy</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you tick "Read my CV to fill this in", your CV is read by Cloudflare's AI (Workers AI) only
      to fill in the form for you to check. It isn't kept by that step, it isn't used to train
      anything, and nothing is read unless you tick the box. A person on our team reads every
      request. For some designs we may build a preview from your details; it stays private to you
      and us until you choose to publish it. Once published, what's on your portfolio is public. If
      you choose "Chat with us instead", your message is handled like any other enquiry (see "If you
      use a form").
    </p>
    <h3>How we keep your data safe</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Everything is sent over an encrypted connection, and stored encrypted by Cloudflare.</li>
      <li>
        Passwords, login sessions and the codes we email are stored only in scrambled form, so even
        we can't read them back. Logging in pauses after five wrong passwords in a row.
      </li>
      <li>
        Your CV and files are kept in private storage with no public address. Only you and the
        Hu/man team can open them, after logging in.
      </li>
      <li>We ask for as little as we need: no street address, no date of birth.</li>
      <li>
        We never sell your data, use it for advertising, or use it to train AI. No decisions with
        legal or similarly significant effects are made about you by automated means.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <h3>How long we keep it</h3>
    <p>
      You can delete your account and everything in it at any time, from your account page. If you
      never confirm your email, the account is deleted after 7 days. If you don't log in for 12
      months, we delete your account and everything in it, unless you've paid for something or your
      site is live, in which case we keep what we need for as long as we host or look after it (then
      12 months more). Invoices and payment records are kept for as long as HMRC requires.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      You can ask what information is held about you, ask for it to be corrected or deleted, or
      raise a concern, by contacting{' '}
      <a href={`mailto:${site.contact.email}`}>{site.contact.email}</a>. We reply within one month.
      If you're not satisfied with the response, you can complain to the UK Information
      Commissioner's Office (ico.org.uk).
    </p>
    <h2>Cookies</h2>
    <p>
      Public pages set no cookies; when you're logged in there is one login cookie. The{' '}
      <a href={withBase('/cookies/')}>cookie policy</a> has the details.
    </p>
  </LegalDoc>

  <TalkBanner />

  <SiteFooter slot="footer" />
</BaseLayout>
